#para(((emph: "bold", text: "D6 Result 1-2 Throw back into combat:"), (emph: "", text: " The victim is hurled back into their own unit like a missile. The victim suffers D3 Strength 6 Hits which Ignores Armour saves, and D6 Strength 3 hits are inflicted on the unit (save as normal). "), (emph: "bold", text: "3-4 Hurl:"), (emph: "", text: " The victim is hurled into an enemy unit within 12\" of the Mammoth – randomly determine which. The victim is removed as a casualty, and the unit takes D6 Strength 3 hits. Unsaved Wounds from these hits count towards the Mammoth's combat result. If no enemy units are in range, treat this as a Throw Back into Combat result instead. "), (emph: "bold", text: "5 Eat:"), (emph: "", text: " The victim model is removed as a casualty, and the Mammoth may immediately recover a single Wound it has lost previously in the game. "), (emph: "bold", text: "6 Squash and grab another:"), (emph: "", text: " The model is removed as a casualty and the Mammoth then picks another victim. Roll again on this table to see what happens.")))
#field("OPTIONS", "")
#items(((runs: ((emph: "", text: "May take light armour +30 points"),), sub: ()),))
#field("NOTES", "")
#items(((runs: ((emph: "", text: "A War Mammoth has a Line of Sight value of 10."),), sub: ()),))

